// (aug14f katana generate lane). The tuple-carried-ref face: a ref in
// a tuple deref'd through .0 inside a recursive fn — the jit
// re-delivered the PRE-WRITE value on the ref-write's propagation
// cycle. The original boundary matrix blamed the tuple (struct- and
// array-carried refs agreed), but the mechanism was the frame-init
// const fire: the framed re-derivation on the write's delivery ran
// the arm regions with init=1, minting FIRED consts. Agrees once the
